Z||000000||72vinman||09-10-2001||10:02 PM||||I removed my plenum today and when I was undoing the nuts for the EGR hose I snapped the screw that was holding the hose to the EGR valve. If I buy a new EGR valve does it replace the whole assembly or do I need to buy the part that hold the EGR seperate. please help I need to get this back together before the GTA Show on Saturday.||||reg||7
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-10-2001||10:30 PM||||If you broke the tube that goes from the EGR valve to the intake, you might get luck and find a new one at the dealer. The new ones are better quality and stronger than the originals. <P>If you broke the bolt that goes into the EGR adapter, you will probably have to carefully drill it out and retap the threads. I don't think the adapter is available at local auto parts stores.<P>Rick 88||||reg||5
Z||000002||72vinman||09-10-2001||10:33 PM||||I broke the bolt that goes into the egr adapter. Is the adapter available from the dealer? Or the junkyard near me has 5 4cyl's, is the EGR adapter the same?<BR>Also while we are on the topic the old heat wrap is in pretty bad shape on the hose. Is there a specific type of heat wrap to use on it?<p>[This message has been edited by 72vinman (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
